Q.3 Scholarship Selection
In a college:
30% of students apply for a scholarship.
70% of students do not apply.
80% of students who apply are selected.
10% of students who do not apply are selected through a special quota.
A randomly selected student is found to be selected.
Find:
Probability that the student applied for the scholarship.
Probability that the student did not apply for the scholarship.
Probability that a selected student had applied for the scholarship.

CODE
P_Apply = 0.30

P_NotApply = 0.70

P_Select_Apply = 0.80

P_Select_NotApply = 0.10

P_Select = (P_Select_Apply * P_Apply) + (P_Select_NotApply * P_NotApply)

P_Apply_Select = (P_Select_Apply * P_Apply) / P_Select

print("Probability that selected student applied for scholarship:")
print(round(P_Apply_Select * 100, 2), "%")

